# Git push

When the user says **"push"**, always:

1. Stage all changes: `git add -A`
2. Commit with a short message (summarize changes or use "Update" if generic)
3. Push to remote: `git push`

Do not only run `git push` and then report uncommitted changes. Commit first, then push. Request `git_write` and `network` permissions when running these commands.
